    "turn_text": "Yeah. Well, look, we have a Democratic Center when it's easy. And leadership means stepping up when it's hard. And she has not been there for that. You know, time and time again when we needed her to take that hard vote to be a Democrat, to preserve at least some really important things for us. She hasn't done it. January 6 happens. We need her to be there in support of the Voting Rights Act. Named after her supposed good friend who she said was her mentor, John Lewis, and she uses the filibuster to stop it. When, you know, You know, the country's workers were hurting, and we wanted to pass a 15-hour minimum wage. She stops that. You know, when we need her to go negotiate for our pharmaceutical prices for our seniors or for just general Americans, she ends up going to go for the pharmaceuticals. So it's easy to be a Democrat when it's the easy votes. We send you to be a leader, and she has not done that. And by the way, You know, when you look at it, there was another senator from Arizona that actually did that and did it correctly and won by even higher margins than cinema did. So even her argument saying that she has to vote this way in order to win reelection is now moot. So what are we looking at? We're looking at someone who, well, now used to be a Democrat because she knew she couldn't beat me in",
