    "turn_text": "first of all, you know, this is assuming obviously she stays in, right? And you don't need a plus one. You have enough to win. But I do think that once we have a fully effective campaign, we're running campaign commercials. We're defining her. We're defining myself. And our name ID is not high, but our favorable is our high. We're going to work on that. Number two, we have a lot of other places that we can actually quote unquote pull from. The average age of a Latino in Arizona is 25. And never in the history of Arizona has there been a young bilingual, well-funded Latino who has grassroots support running in Arizona. And we're going to work that and we're going to work it like it's nobody's business. And we're going to have margins there that people have not seen ever in Arizona. And they're never going to go for a cinema. They're not going to go for any of the Republicans, no matter who they put pull up. Number two, I think at the end of the day, whatever independence she does have in terms of support, once they understand how she works for Wall Street, once she understands how she works for the pharmaceutical industry. Once they understand how she didn't stand with us in defending democracy, I don't see her getting much of that independent leading democratic support. And then for Republicans, we're not going to be able to win many Republicans. But for those Republicans that believe in national security, believe in democracy, they're not going to take",
