  {
    "episode_id": 94498,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/4/94498.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 43,
    "turn_text": "Yes, they're there. And it's not just Carrie Lake. This is something that's really taken over a lot of the really, really base of the Republican Party. I do work with a lot of Republicans to be honest here. In Congress, in regards to Ukraine, they're actually very supportive. They're what I like to call the pro-freedom caucus. But in terms of some of the voters, they are listening to Tucker Carlson, they're listening to Donald Trump, and they care more about the partisan end result of stopping Ukraine from succeeding because it's another way to kind of get the lids, right, or own the lids. But the history of the Democratic Party and the Republican Party is to make sure that we ensure freedom all around the world. And there isn't really a black and white here. Look, and there have been black and white situations in other times in terms of when we've been engaged when we've been engaging ourselves. But there is no black and white here. Ukraine is a free and democratic country that had its sovereign borders invaded multiple times. And even though we clearly warned Russia, we clearly warned the world that this was happening. They still proceeded and they're not only proceeded but have proceeded with massive, massive humanitarian violations and war crimes. And for us, for us as a country to see this happening in front of our eyes and actually contemplate pulling away weaponry from them so they could at least at a minimum defend themselves is disgusting. It would be such a black mark on our history in our nation if we did that, especially again when this is a truly black and white situation. There is such a thing as good and evil in this world and right now the way that the Russian government, maybe not necessarily the people and the military are conducting themselves with Putin. They are acting in an evil manner and we should be proud to stand with good people that just want freedom.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
